# HELD pending coordinated disclosure to StarkWare (HANDOFF.md §5).
# These are ignored, not merely untracked, so `git add -A` cannot sweep them
# into a public commit by accident — which is exactly how packages/skills and
# packages/mcp were published in 8ec0c9e.
findings/
upstream-prs/
claude-docs/
devtool/packages/skills/
devtool/packages/mcp/

# Internal working notes, same class as CLAUDE.md and the docs above: they steer the
# work, they are not the work. Ignored rather than merely untracked for the same reason
# as the block above — `git add -A` should not be able to sweep them into a public commit.
OPEN-QUESTIONS.md
ANSWERS.md

# Third-party STRK20 agent skills, installed via:
#   npx skills add welttowelt/strk20-skills
# 312K of upstream documentation bundled verbatim. Ignored rather than vendored
# because it is reinstallable in one command and is not our work. To vendor it
# instead (self-contained clones), delete this line and `git add .agents/`.
.agents/
.upstream/
# Copied in by devtool's `prepack` and removed by `postpack` — npm auto-includes README and
# LICENSE only from the package root, and both live at the repo root by deliberate choice
# (E-PUB2, claude-docs/DECISIONS-NEEDED.md D4). Ignored so an interrupted pack cannot commit a
# second copy of either.
devtool/README.md
devtool/LICENSE

# web/ — the marketing site.
#
# `NON-Natural-Grotesk-Regular.woff2` is licensed to the author for PERSONAL USE. That covers
# building this site; it does not cover redistributing the file, and committing a font to a
# repository is redistribution regardless of what the site does with it. `web/scripts/preflight.ts`
# fails the build with the path and an explanation when it is absent, so a missing licence is a
# clear error rather than a wordmark quietly set in the fallback face. See web/README.md.
#
# The other three faces (Geist, Geist Mono, Instrument Serif) are OFL and ARE committed.
web/public/fonts/NON-Natural-Grotesk-Regular.woff2

# The mark is Marvel's HYDRA insignia. Same treatment as the font and for a stronger reason:
# it is a third party's trademark, not a licence the author holds. The site builds with it in
# place; the repository does not carry it. Copy it to `web/public/hydra.svg` to build, and see
# web/README.md before this is published anywhere.
web/public/hydra.svg
web/app/icon.svg

web/.next/
web/out/
web/next-env.d.ts
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
